sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User (Dev/Business)
    participant Jira
    participant CodeValidation as Code Validation Service (Python)
    participant GitHub as GitHub / GCS
    participant CodeAnalyser as Static Code Analyser
    participant Gemini as Gemini API
    participant DocGenerator as Documentation Generation Service (Python)
    participant GCS as Google Cloud Storage (Archive)
    participant Confluence as Confluence API

    Note over User, Jira: 1. Initiation

    User->>+Jira: Create Documentation Request Ticket (link to GitHub / GCS file)
    Jira-->>-User: Ticket Created

    Note over Jira, Gemini: 2. Trigger Code Validation

    Jira->>+CodeValidation: Trigger Workflow (e.g., webhook, polling)
    Note over CodeValidation: Reads Ticket for details (GitHub / GCS file)
    
    CodeValidation->>+GitHub: Fetch Code (Python / Jupyter Notebook)
    GitHub-->>-CodeValidation: Return Code Content
    
    CodeValidation->>+CodeAnalyser: Verify code
    CodeAnalyser-->>-CodeValidation: Return verification result    

    CodeValidation->>+Gemini: Request Code Validation
    Note right of Gemini: Evaluates the form of the code and documentation completeness
    Gemini-->>-CodeValidation: Return validation result

    CodeValidation->>+Jira: Update ticket with validation result and change status 
    deactivate CodeValidation

    Jira->>+User: Notify User about the validation result

    Note over User, GCS: 3. Documentation Generation

    User->>+Jira: Update ticket for Release (link to GitHub / GCS file)
    Jira-->>-User: Send ticket update notification

    Jira->>+DocGenerator: Start documentation generation

    DocGenerator->>+GitHub: Fetch Code (Python / Jupyter Notebook)
    GitHub-->>-DocGenerator: Return Code Content
    
    DocGenerator->>+Gemini: Request Documentation Generation (send code)
    Note right of Gemini: Generates documentation based on code
    Gemini-->>-DocGenerator: Return Generated Documentation (as file/content)

    Note over DocGenerator, Confluence: 5. Confluence Update

    DocGenerator->>+GCS: Find the last existing documentation for this file
    GCS-->>-DocGenerator: return the last stored version
    DocGenerator->>+GCS: Store the generated documentation as the next version

    DocGenerator->>+Confluence: Update Existing Page / Create New Page (include the version number from GCS)
        alt Update/Create Fails
            Confluence-->>DocGenerator: Error Response
            Note right of DocGenerator: Implement Retry Logic
            DocGenerator-->>Confluence: Retry Update/Create
        end
    Confluence-->>-DocGenerator: Success Confirmation (after success/retries)

    Note over DocGenerator, Jira: 6. Finalization

    DocGenerator-->>Jira: Update Ticket Status with new Confluence link
    Jira-->>-User: Notify User about documentation
